From 1d13c88d2e57bc63ce1586fe0b8f3342b6afdd19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mlgprorektm8 <67933lance@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:51:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FIX-188: #65's Intel Arc changes on Intel GPUs only

Brings back the Intel Arc work reverted in the commit before, each change behind
Instance::IsIntel() (vendor 0x8086); every other GPU keeps what it had:
- translation: memory-only compute barriers, 64-bit shared memory as two
  32-bit halves (Profile.intel_arc_workarounds); the NVIDIA-only
  explicit-layout change is dropped
- 32-wide compute subgroups, pipelineCreationCacheControl and
  computeFullSubgroups
- cached host memory for imported host memory (RHI and direct memory)
- 256 MB stream rings and device-local staging blocks; command thread
  synced before arena binds
- session ended (native splice, barrier flush) before the submit callback;
  native work recorded into the scheduler's command buffer, compute
  pipelines bound on every dispatch
- tile manager descriptor ranges clamped, at least one group dispatched
Not brought back: direct memory off and SanitizeCopyLayers undone (the
patch's older base), the window raise in sdl_window. Kept for all, no
effect in normal use: null-pipeline draw skips, optional RHI Invalidate
and WrapCommandBuffer, the diagnostic probes' host barriers.

Co-Authored-By: Gabriel Foss <RidgeBridgeStudios@users.noreply.github.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
